title: BITTER PapRAT Scheduled Tasks and C2 Domains on Command Line
id: 97a1e587-3a0c-4329-93b5-6996643c1904
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects BITTER/TA397 PapRAT tradecraft documented by FortiGuard: scheduled
    tasks named MicrosoftUpdates\updates11678 and BiosUpdates\update101, and
    command lines that reference the campaign's staging files (err.log,
    talk.log) or hardcoded PapRAT/WmRAT command-and-control domains.
references:
    - https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/bitter-expands-its-arsenal-with-paprat
    - https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/paprat-bitter-cyberespionage/
    - https://gbhackers.com/paprat-malware/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/03
tags:
    - attack.t1053
    - attack.t1036
    - attack.t1071
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_scheduled_task:
        Image|endswith: '\schtasks.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'MicrosoftUpdates\updates11678'
            - 'BiosUpdates\update101'
    selection_c2_domain:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'goodnfortunes.com'
            - 'techtalkhelp.com'
            - 'rivingtonclarks.com'
            - 'netmansrvdns.com'
            - 'rappellingaart.com'
            - 'gomescareerplans.com'
            - 'chestergreenfarming.com'
    selection_staging_file:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'C:\users\public\music\err.log'
            - 'C:\programdata\talk.log'
    condition: selection_scheduled_task or selection_c2_domain or selection_staging_file
falsepositives:
    - None expected; task names, staging paths, and C2 domains are campaign-specific
level: high
